e sine function has a period of \\( 360^\\circ \\) or \\( 2\\pi \\) radians, and the sine function is symmetric about \\( 90^\\circ \\).\n\nFirst, recall the conversion between degrees and radians:\n\\[\n1^\\circ = \\frac{\\pi}{180} \\text{ radians}\n\\]\nThus, \\( x \\) degrees is equivalent to \\( \\frac{\\pi x}{180} \\) radians.\n\nWe need to solve:\n\\[\n\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{180}\\right) = \\sin(x)\n\\]\n\nThe sine function has the property:\n\\[\n\\sin(\\theta) = \\sin(\\pi - \\theta)\n\\]\nThus, we have two cases to consider:\n1. \\(\\frac{\\pi x}{180} = x + 2k\\pi\\) for some integer \\( k \\)\n2. \\(\\frac{\\pi x}{180} = \\pi - x + 2k\\pi\\) for some integer \\( k \\)\n\n### Case 1: \\(\\frac{\\pi x}{180} = x + 2k\\pi\\)\n\nRearrange this equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi x}{180} - x = 2k\\pi\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{180} - 1 \\right) = 2k\\pi\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\left( \\frac{\\pi - 180}{180} \\right) = 2k\\pi\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{2k \\cdot 180 \\pi}{\\pi - 180}\n\\]\n\nFor the smallest positive \\( x \\), set \\( k = 1 \\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{360\\pi}{\\pi - 180}\n\\]\n\n### Case 2: \\(\\frac{\\pi x}{180} = \\pi - x + 2k\\pi\\)\n\nRearrange this equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi x}{180} + x = \\pi + 2k\\pi\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{180} + 1 \\right) = (2k+1)\\pi\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\left( \\frac{\\pi + 180}{180} \\right) = (2k+1)\\pi\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{180(2k+1)\\pi}{\\pi + 180}\n\\]\n\nFor the smallest positive \\( x \\), set \\( k = 0 \\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{180\\pi}{\\pi + 180}\n\\]\n\nThus, the two least positive values of \\( x \\) are:\n\\[\nx_1 = \\frac{360\\pi}{\\pi - 180} = \\frac{360\\pi}{180 - \\pi} = \\frac{2\\pi}{1 - \\frac{\\pi}{180}} = \\frac{2\\pi}{1 - \\frac{\\pi}{180}} = \\frac{360\\pi}{180 - \\pi}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_2 = \\frac{180\\pi}{\\pi + 180}\n\\]\n\nRewriting in the form \\(\\frac{m\\pi}{n-\\pi}\\) and \\(\\frac{p\\pi}{q+\\pi}\\):\n\\[\nx_1 = \\frac{360\\pi}{180 - \\pi} = \\frac{360\\pi}{180 - \\pi} \\quad \\text{(already in form)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_2 = \\frac{180\\pi}{180 + \\pi}\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( m = 360 \\), \\( n = 180 \\), \\( p = 180 \\), \\( q = 180 \\).\n\nSumming these values:\n\\[\nm + n + p + q = 360 + 180 + 180 + 180 = 900\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{900}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{900}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
